    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d222">

                <pb facs="0215" n="205" xml:id="pg205"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.01/11–2949: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in France</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Bruce</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Paris</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-11-29T20:00:00+01:00">November 29,
                            1949—8 p. m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 11 p. m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>5022. Foreign Office confirms information given London’s 933, November 28,<anchor
                        n="48" xml:id="d222-f1"/> regarding Vatican’s desire extend early
                    recognition Chinese Communists. Foreign Office states Vatican reluctant to take
                    lead, however, and is endeavoring to persuade some prominent Catholic country
                    break the ice. French position, however, remains unchanged (Embtel 4790,
                    November 16).</p>
                <p>Sent Department 5022, repeated London 876.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bruce</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d222-f1" n="48" xml:id="d222-f1-content">
                <p>Same as telegram No. 4731, November 28, 5 p. m., from London, <ref
                        target="#pg203">p. 203</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
